  "term": "hysterical disorder",
  "definition": "In this historical source, hysterical disorder refers to a wide-ranging disturbance affecting both bodily nervous functions and mental life, especially feeling, without any demonstrable bodily disease to account for it. It is described as arising from nervous instability together with internal or external stress, often showing mainly physical symptoms despite an underlying mental element.",
